1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Maharana Pratap or Pratap Singh of Mewar (May 9, 1540 – January 29, 1597) was a Hindu ruler of Mewar, a state in north-western India. He belonged to the Sisodia clan of Suryavanshi Rajputs. The epitome of fiery Raj
2 CONC put pride and self-respect, Pratap has for centuries exemplified the qualities to which Rajputs aspire.
2 CONT
