1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Era: Late 19th century (circa 1870s–1900s)
2 CONT Role: Qazi like his father, but also engaged in some local governance and tax mediation with British authorities.
2 CONT Location: Continued Rawalpindi region presence, with increasing connections to Mirpur (Azad Kashmir) through kinship networks and administrative posts.
2 CONT Notable: He is said to have had nephews or close relatives serving in Mirpur tehsil as Qazis, helping maintain Ratyal Mughal influence there. This indicates a branching out of family influence eastward.
