1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sawai Bhawani Singh Bahadur was the last titular Maharaja of Jaipur and head of the Kachwaha clan of Rajputs. The title technically ended when royal entitlements were abolished along with privy purses through a con
2 CONC stitutional amendment in 1971. However, the erstwhile maharaja is considered a political, cultural, and religious icon in modern Rajasthan, and he is sometimes still referred to in the media as His Highness, The Maharaja of Jaipur
2 CONC .
