1 NOTE {geni:about_me} " Both of Tale Yar Khan's sons had come here on leave. Then the Mutiny prevented them from leaving,and they stayed on here. After Delhi was re-taken both of them were hanged,though they had committed no crime.Tale 
2 CONC Yar Khan is in Tonk. He is alive,but I am certain that he would be better off dead."
2 CONT
2 CONT Above is excerpts from Mirza Ghalib's letter to Shafaq reviewing the whole Delhi scene.Source: Page 243: Book GHALIB(1797-1869),VOL. I,LIFE & LETTERS,translated & edited by Ralph Russell & Khurshid Alam; George Allen & Unwin Ltd.,
2 CONC Ruskin House,,Museum street,London;Printed by Unwin Brothers Limited,The Gresham Press,Old Working Surrey,England;First published in 1969;UNESCO coolection; Account no. 565117 in Delhi Public Library, S.P.Mukerji Marg,Delhi I hear
2 CONC d that he was travelling somewhere near Red Fort when opposite it he was provoked to see a British police officer mercilessly thrashing old native man and then he threw his key ring in such manner that it hit the temple of the pol
2 CONC ice officer that the police officer died instantly. My great grandfather was identified by keychain & hanged to death along with his brother Asghar Yar Khan at huge peepal tree at Purani Kotwali near Gurudwara Sis Ganj,Chandni Cho
2 CONC wk,Delhi. 
