1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sayyid Babar Ali Khan Bahadur (Bengali: বাবর আলী খান; died 28 April 1810) was the Nawab of Bengal and Bihar. He succeeded to the Nawab's Masnad (throne) after his father, Mubarak Ali Khan (Nawab of Bengal) died on 
2 CONC 6 September 1793. He reigned from 1793 until 1810, when he died on 28 April 1810.
2 CONT Life
2 CONT Nawab Nazim Babar Ali Khan was born to Mubarak Ali Khan (Nawab of Bengal) and Faiz-un-nisa Walida Begum, one of his principal wives. Babar Ali Khan succeeded his father to the Masnad (throne) after he died on 6 September 1793.
2 CONT
2 CONT Death and succession
2 CONT Nawab Nazim Babar Ali Khan died on 28 April 1810 and was succeeded by his elder son, Zain-ud-Din Ali Khan as Nawab of Bengal and Bihar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wives and children
2 CONT Nawab Nazim Babar Ali Khan had two wives. His first wife was Babbu Begum Sahiba. She was the daughter of Muhammad Sami Khan. The name of Babar Ali Khan's second wife is unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT Babar Ali had two sons. Zain-ud-Din Ali Khan was the eldest son of Babar Ali by Babbu Begum and Ahmad Ali Khan was his youngest son by his second wife.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babar_Ali_Khan
