1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Nawab of Bengal and Bihar.
2 CONT Zain-ud-Din Ali Khan (died 6 August 1821), better known as Ali Jah was the Nawab of Bengal and Bihar. He succeeded his father, Baber Ali Khan after his death on 28 April 1810.[1] He was succeeded by his half-brother, Ahmad Ali Kha
2 CONC n, after his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Zain-ud-Din, was the eldest son of Baber Ali Khan by his wife, Babbu Begum. His coronation was on 5 June 1810.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 6 August 1821, leaving only three daughters but no son. He was succeeded by his half-brother, Ahmad Ali Khan.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ali_Jah
