2 TITL amma
2 NOTE Death on a Friday or in Ramadhan
3 CONT 15Dec
3 CONT 2012
3 CONT
3 CONT 0 Comment
3 CONT
3 CONT There is a common belief that one who passes away during blessed days or months is saved from the punishment of the grave.
3 CONT
3 CONT The following discussion supports this.
3 CONT
3 CONT
3 CONT Death on a Friday
3 CONT
3 CONT Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Amr ibn al-‘As (radiyallahu ánhuma) reports that Rasulullah (sallallahu álaihi Wasallam) said, ‘Whoever passes away on a Friday will be saved from the punishment of the grave.’
3 CONT
3 CONT (Musnad Ahmad vol.2 pg.220; hadith 7050, 6646).
3 CONT
3 CONT Similar narrations have been reported by Sayyiduna Jabir ibn Abdullah
3 CONT
3 CONT (refer Hilyat al-Awliya vol.3 pg.181),
3 CONT
3 CONT Sayyiduna Anas ibn Malik (refer Abu Ya’ala, Majma al-Zawa’id vol.2 pg.319)
3 CONT
3 CONT and others. see: Al-Maqasidul Hasanah, Hadith:1186
3 CONT
3 CONT Meaning of this Hadith
3 CONT
3 CONT It is possible that the punishment is withheld for that day or even permanently. (Fatawa Mahmudiyya vol.6 pg.62; Rad al-Muhtar vol.2 pg.165)
