2 FILE https://media.geni.com/p13/d8/9d/64/2c/53444839afde1827/amma_original.jpg?hash=12ba67ef937eef7d4cad8a07aa6a8d7f211f61e038de9bf395156db1703d6bf9.1797148799
2 FORM jpg
2 NOTE Your beauty is aptly narrated in this poem of Amir Khusro which was also one of your favorites, my beloved mother
3 CONT "Ay chehra-e zeba-e tu rashk-e butan-e azari;
3 CONT Har chand wasfat mikunam dar husn-az-aan zebatari.
3 CONT Aafaq ra gar deedah am mehr-e butan warzeedah am;
3 CONT Bisyar khuban deedah am lekin tu cheez-e degari.
3 CONT Man tu shudam, tu man shudi, man tan shudam, tu jan shudi;
3 CONT Taakas nagoyad baad azeen man deegaram tu deegari.
3 CONT Khusrau ghareeb ast-o gada uftadah dar shehr-e shuma;
3 CONT Baashad ki az behr-e khuda, su-e ghareeban bangari."
3 CONT (Translation of aforementioned in English language)
3 CONT O you whose beautiful face is the envy of the idols of Azar
3 CONT (Abraham's father and famous idol maker);
3 CONT You remain superior to my praise.
3 CONT All over the world have I traveled;
3 CONT many a maiden’s love have I tasted;
3 CONT Many a beauty-star have I seen; but you are something unique.
3 CONT I have become you, and you me; I have become the body,
3 CONT you the soul; So that none hereafter may say 
3 CONT that “I am someone and you someone else.”
3 CONT Khusro a beggar, a stranger has come wandering to your town;
3 CONT For the sake of god, have pity on this beggar 
3 CONT and do not turn him away from your door.
