1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Brigadier (Retd.) Mirza Hamid Hussain (July 4, 1914-August 12, 1987) was born in 1914 at Delhi. He was educated at Aligarh Muslim University, Aligarh and the 'Prince of Wales' Royal Military College RIMC, Dehra Dun
2 CONC . He was commissioned from the Indian Military Academy in the first batch of 1934 and was attached to a British Battalion, The King's Shropshire Light Infantry. He later joined the 47th Sikh regiment. He saw active service on the 
2 CONC Frontier Waziristan Operation where he was mentioned in Dispatches for gallant and distinguished service in the field.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the first and senior most Indian Commissioned Officers to join the Indian Army Ordnance Corps in 1940. He served in Iraq and Iran in various senior appointments DADOD 10th Army and Chief Ordnance Officer. He graduated from 
2 CONC Staff College, Quetta, in 1945 and commanded various Ordnance Depots in India. He was then appointed ADOS in G.H.Q. India where he was in charge of Operation and training the Ordnance Service.
2 CONT
2 CONT On partition, he opted for Pakistan Army and came to Pakistan as Deputy Director Ordnance Service G.H.Q. Rawalpindi. Later he was appointed Director of Weapon and Equipment in The General Staff Branch G.H.Q. and subsequently took 
2 CONC over as Director of Staff Duties. On completion of tenure, he was appointed Director of Inter-Services Intelligence, Karachi. He was selected for Foreign Service in 1951 and was appointed Deputy Secretary in the Ministry of Foreig
2 CONC n affairs in charge of the Middle East Division. Later, he became Chief of Protocol. In 1952 he was selected for the appointment of Counselor, Pakistan High Commission, London. He has been counselor in Iraq, Iran and Turkey. He ha
2 CONC s been Chare d'Affairs as Joint secretary, Chief of Protocol. He has been honored with the 'Order of Monrovia’ and 'Membership of the Civil Merit' from Spain.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is a direct descendant of Nawab Qasim Khan who came to India from Yarkand. He died in 1987 at the age of 73 in Lahore
