1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * Profile picture - William; in foreground, with his sister Catherine. By George Chinnery c1804.
2 CONT * Painted in India before they were baptised in London 25/3/1805, their names (their father James having converted to the Shia faith) were Mir Ghulam Ali, Sahib Allum and Noor-un-Nissa, Sahiba Begum.
2 CONT
2 CONT the Kirkpatrick family has documented Y-DNA haplogroups within E1b1b, specifically subclades such as E-BY5766, E-CTS5856, and E-V13
2 CONT
2 CONT The Kirkpatrick surname has been the subject of various genealogical and genetic studies. According to the Kirkpatrick/Kilpatrick DNA Project hosted by Family Tree DNA, individuals bearing the Kirkpatrick surname predominantly bel
2 CONC ong to the R1b haplogroup, particularly the subclade R-BY71936
