1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * 1st Indian Barrister in Bombay, April 1867.
2 CONT * 1st Indian to hold the post of Chief Justice in Bombay, 1902.
2 CONT * 1st Muslim to become the "President of Indian National Congress", Mysore, 1887.
2 CONT * 3rd President of the Indian National Congress (INC), Mysore, 1887.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji] was the son of Cambay (''Khambat'') business merchant, [http://www.geni.com/people/Al-Haj-Mulla-Aamil-Al-Hadd-ul-Faazil-Tyab-Ali-bin-Bhai-Miyan/60
2 CONC 00000011253275166/ Mulla Tyab Ali bin Bhai Miyan], and his wife, [http://www.geni.com/people/Ameena-binte-Mulla-Meher-Ali/6000000011253629327/ Ameena], the daughter of a rich ''Mulla'', [http://www.geni.com/people/Al-Hadd-ul-Faazi
2 CONC l-Raas-ul-Hudood-Mulla-Meher-Ali-bin-Shaikh-Ibrahim/6000000011253591499/ Mulla Meher Ali]. All of [http://www.geni.com/people/Al-Haj-Mulla-Aamil-Al-Hadd-ul-Faazil-Tyab-Ali-bin-Bhai-Miyan/6000000011253275166/ Tyab Ali's] sons went 
2 CONC to England for further education or trade. His elder brother, [http://www.geni.com/people/Camaruddin-Tyabji/6000000002006945474/ Camaruddin], had been the first Indian solicitor admitted in England, and inspired the 15-year-old [h
2 CONC ttp://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin] to join the Bar. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In April 1860, [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji] went to England to study at the Highbury New Park College. His father gave him letters of introduction to [http://www.geni.com/peop
2 CONC le/Edward-Law-1st-Earl-of-Ellenborough-GCB/6000000011226168404/ Lord Ellenborough], the retired Viceroy of India. [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji] passed the London matriculation 
2 CONC examination and entered London University and the Middle Temple as a student in 1863. Because of deteriorating eyesight he returned to Bombay in late 1864 but resumed terms at the Middle Temple in late 1865. While in India he was 
2 CONC married to a 14-year-old girl, [http://www.geni.com/people/Rahat-un-Nafs-Tyabji/6000000011253395566/ Rahat-un-Nafs binte Sharaf Ali]. He was called to the Bar in April 1867, and on his return to Bombay in December 1867 became the 
2 CONC first Indian barrister in the High Court of Bombay.
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji] was elected to the municipal corporation in 1873. He was a member of the University of Bombay senate (1875–1905) and appointed to the Bombay legis
2 CONC lative council in 1882, resigning in 1886 owing to ill health. Along with Pherozeshah Mehta and K. T. Telang, he was largely responsible for forming the Bombay Presidency Association in 1885, a body which championed Indian interes
2 CONC ts and hosted the first meeting of the Indian National Congress in Bombay at the end of 1885. [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji] was the third President of Congress. He was deeply c
2 CONC oncerned with matters affecting Muslims. To promote social interaction among the city's Muslims, [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Tyabji] was instrumental in founding both the Islam Club and the Is
2 CONC lam Gymkhana. He sent all of his daughters to be educated in Bombay and in 1904 he sent two of them to boarding school in Haslemere in England.
2 CONT
2 CONT In June 1895, [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji] was made a judge of the Bombay High Court, the first Muslim and the third Indian to be so elevated. While on a year's furlough in Lo
2 CONC ndon in 1906, [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji] died suddenly of a heart attack.
2 CONT
