1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Youngest of [http://www.geni.com/people/Badruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253322961/ Badruddin Tyabji's] brothers. Him and his wife [http://www.geni.com/people/Hamida-binte-Haider-Ali-Hakim/6000000011358533705/ Hamida Beg
2 CONC um] (D/o [http://www.geni.com/people/Haider-Ali-Hakim-bin-Fateh-Ali/6000000014082828621/ Haider Ali Hakim] of Surat) were childless and lived at '''Khetwadi''', South Bombay (Current day; '''Grant Road'''), where the '''Tyabji''' 
2 CONC family owned several family plots. They took charge of raising several of the Jama'at (Community's) orphans and under-privileged. 
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://www.geni.com/people/Dr-Salim-Ali/6000000011501253872/ Dr. Salim Moizuddin Ali], the famous birdman of India, was one of them. He was brought up by this maternal uncle, [http://www.geni.com/people/Amiruddin-Tyabji/600000001
2 CONC 1253403124/ Amiruddin Tyabji]. The latter was a keen ''Shikari'' (Hunter) and a nature-lover. Under his guidance young [http://www.geni.com/people/Dr-Salim-Ali/6000000011501253872/ Dr. Salim Ali] learnt his first lessons in ''Shik
2 CONC ar'' (Hunt) and became aware of the nature around him. [http://www.geni.com/people/Amiruddin-Tyabji/6000000011253403124/ Amiruddin] later sent the young boy to the '''Bombay Natural History Society (BNHS)'''. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 1: [http://www.geni.com/people/Dr-Salim-Ali/6000000011501253872/ Dr. Salim Ali] websites, "The Fall of a Sparrow" - Autobiography by [http://www.geni.com/people/Dr-Salim-Ali/6000000011501253872/ Dr. Salim Ali], and self.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source 2: Prof. Theodore P. Wright Jr.'s Tyabji Clan Family Charts (1970)
