1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was the seventy-fourth ruler of the Mewar Dynasty (r. 1930-1955) and he succeeded his father Maharana FATEH SINGH. He ruled from Udaipur. Bhupal was the first natural-born son of the Mewar family to succeed to t
2 CONC he throne in almost one hundred years, after five consecutive adoptions.
2 CONT
2 CONT Maharana Bhupal Singh as the ruler of Mewar guided its destiny through India’s most momentous period, the Independence from British Imperial rule...
2 CONT
