1 OCCU Chief Justice of Baroda High Court, Freedom Fighter
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * '''Chief Justice of Baroda High Court'''
2 CONT * [http://www.geni.com/people/Mahatma-Gandhi-%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE/6000000003922874202/ Mahatma Gandhi's] right-hand at the ''Salt March'' at Dandi, Gujarat in 1930 AD.
2 CONT * Wilaadat (Birth): 4th Jamaadil Awwal 1270 AH (1st February 1854 AD)
2 CONT * Wafaat (Death): 20th Rabi' ul-Awwal 1355 AH (9th June 1936 AD)
2 CONT
2 CONT Abbas Tyabji (died June 9th, 1936) was an Indian freedom fighter from Gujarat, who had served as the Chief Justice of the Baroda High Court. He was a key ally and supporter of Sardar Vallabhbhai Patel during the 1918 Kheda Satyagr
2 CONC aha, and the 1928 Bardoli Satyagraha. He was also a close supporter of [http://www.geni.com/people/Mahatma-Gandhi-%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5%8D%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE/6000000003922874202/ Mohandas Gandhi] and the Indian
2 CONC  National Congress. In 1919-20, Abbas Tyabji was one of the members of the Committee appointed by the Indian National Congress to review the charges against General Reginald Dyer for the Amritsar Jallianwala Bagh Massacre, which o
2 CONC ccurred during the fight for independence from the British. Tyabji became the national leader after leading major protests against the arrest of [http://www.geni.com/people/Mahatma-Gandhi-%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%B9%E0%A4%BE%E0%A4%A4%E0%A5
2 CONC %8D%E0%A4%AE%E0%A4%BE/6000000003922874202/ Mohandas Gandhi] in May 1930. He died in Mussoorie (now in Uttaranchal) on June 9, 1936.
2 CONT
